                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "33abff8e-5ea9-3042-83e9-d49f3075d1f7",
                        "entry_id": "223b75c4-df87-35ba-b0e7-9de4f1082135",
                        "glosses": [
                            "North Atlantic Treaty Organization, zu deutsch Nordatlantikvertrag-Organisation"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "0b8ceab5-0a9c-4019-b0bf-0e786bbfcbdd",
                                "sense_id": "33abff8e-5ea9-3042-83e9-d49f3075d1f7",
                                "text": "Die NATO wurde 1949 gegründet und hat heute ihren Sitz in Brüssel."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "31e28688-455b-4183-b8cb-0d0d388639e2",
                                "sense_id": "33abff8e-5ea9-3042-83e9-d49f3075d1f7",
                                "text": "„In Brüssel trafen sich die Verteidigungsminister der NATO zu einem eilig einberufenen Sondergipfel.“"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "4497ac40-2a05-42d1-b3bf-705a3a4f3320",
                                "sense_id": "33abff8e-5ea9-3042-83e9-d49f3075d1f7",
                                "text": "„Da nirgendwo verlässlich niedergeschrieben ist, wie oft CIA, Pentagon oder NATO in schweinebuchtähnliche Situationen geraten sind und wie sie sich dann verhalten haben, können die beiden jetzt ewig weiterstreiten.“"
                            }
                        ],
                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e4e7740e-949b-43a2-a81a-8aa6680e6f9a",
                        "source_entry_id": "223b75c4-df87-35ba-b0e7-9de4f1082135",
                        "source_sense_id": "33abff8e-5ea9-3042-83e9-d49f3075d1f7",
                        "target_lang_word": "NATO",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "NATO",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                        "entry_id": "57342c09-5694-31f4-ad37-92ae97be7569",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Acronym of North Atlantic Treaty Organization"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "abbreviation",
                                            "acronym",
                                            "alt-of"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a0ce5a4a-6721-4b13-9b29-281d1340e718",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "On the other hand, one still would have to note that relations between NATO in London and OSR in Paris were still not as closely integrated as might be desired, and that the power of decision, especially on industrial and financial matters, still was not centered in one place in the NATO."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "26603c31-466e-457b-adaa-c87824448774",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "Yes, France is geographically situated in a key position so far as Western Europe is concerned. They are really the bridge between Germany, Spain and Italy. And it was necessary to have a NATO organization that was unified and France was a necessary member of that organization."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "84f92b06-fcaf-4f4c-be2e-42f0fa3742d8",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "What concerned me most about De Gaulle's decision was that it threatened the unity of NATO, which had been so carefully developed over two decades. NATO was essential to the security of Europe and the United States. I was convinced that the stronger and more unified we were, the more incentive the Soviets and their Warsaw Pact allies would have to work with us in solving outstanding problems and differences."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "cbc1a9ab-15f3-4917-86fb-0468669257c6",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "President Putin's KGB roots have sadly informed a style of governance that is neither reformist nor particularly democratic. The common thread throughout his domestic and foreign policies is his effort to trade on fear -- the fears of Russians that their country is under attack from hostile external forces (Chechens, NATO or free marketeers); and the fears of Westerners that if not for a strong, pragmatic leader, Russia will again become unruly, unstable and potentially aggressive."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "67ae1e74-01ff-4d72-b3bb-a8142dbbbcb3",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "In the week since I’d seen him in the Oval Office, Bush had done well in Europe.[...]He’d made a strong statement on the expansion of NATO. “I believe in membership,” the president had said, “for all of Europe’s democracies that seek it and are ready to share the responsibilities that NATO brings.”[…]The president had even gone out of his way to reassure Putin that he had nothing to fear from the enlargement of NATO, which would not include Russia."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "af07bf78-a0ee-4ad6-8760-8651dc3d192d",
                                                "sense_id": "ecd26766-bee4-3bc6-a956-781565e85cef",
                                                "text": "Trump’s grotesque and incomprehensible fondness for Putin makes the details of any deal highly dangerous for Europe and the NATO alliance, founded to confront Russia."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "NATO",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "4f96738a-7222-3f22-895e-4739f2b86a6f",
